{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300206-adversaries-the-quaghead-tribe-and-boscu-hundred-devils-metody","id":1300206,"title":"Adversaries: The Quaghead Tribe and Boscu & Hundred Devils: Metody","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-26T23:41:07-07:00","id":1300206,"title":"Adversaries: The Quaghead Tribe and Boscu & Hundred Devils: Metody","content":"Adversaries: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/264800/Adversaries-of-the-Righteous-The-Quaghead-Tribe\" target=\"_blank\">The Quaghead Tribe</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/264217/Adversaries-of-the-Righteous-Boscu-Prodigal-Son-of-the-Swamps\" target=\"_blank\">Boscu</a>, their runaway scion.<br /> <br /> Hundred Devils: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/264799/Hundred-Devils-Night-Parade-Metody\" target=\"_blank\">Metody</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T01:49:14-07:00","id":1300218,"title":"","content":"The Quaghead Tribe and Boscu are honestly two of my favourite additions to this collection to date, and I've loved a lot of them. Just bursting with story hooks and cool setting material to add into a campaign. Crocodile-riding bayou bandits descended from an ancient magically enforced legalistic kingdom! Great stuff.<br /> <br /> Tiny minor quibble that I mainly found amusing: there is NO way Boscu as illustrated looks like a teenager, dude has some road miles on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":1079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","user":"Megapope","date":". 03-27-2019, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:03:00-07:00","id":1300234,"title":"","content":"You know, I've always imagined vitriol to be a green liquid. I'd be interested to go back and see if it was ever described as such, or I was just presuming from the general colour tones of Malfeas. Certainly, there's something fitting in it being a more nasty, muddy colour.<br /> <br /> As for the metody itself, that's a nice looking demon, and a good validation in my eyes of using these more invested write-ups to make for more effective realisations of the concepts attributed to several spirits. The Rival Nature Subsumption Merit in particular has staggering implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T08:04:52-07:00","id":1300281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300206-adversaries-the-quaghead-tribe-and-boscu-hundred-devils-metody?p=1300234#post1300234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've always imagined vitriol to be a green liquid. I'd be interested to go back and see if it was ever described as such, or I was just presuming from the general colour tones of Malfeas. Certainly, there's something fitting in it being a more nasty, muddy colour.<br /> <br /> As for the metody itself, that's a nice looking demon, and a good validation in my eyes of using these more invested write-ups to make for more effective realisations of the concepts attributed to several spirits. The Rival Nature Subsumption Merit in particular has staggering implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcannon for vitriol was always the green acid stuff from DOOM 1&amp;2. Even if there's no basis for that in the text, I don't know if I'll ever be able to separate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T08:20:12-07:00","id":1300287,"title":"","con