,"signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T20:59:36-07:00","id":1300463,"title":"","content":"Do you think rival nature subsumption could allow a Metody to pick up a solar excellency charm? <br /> I'm imagining a really powerful old Metody who at one time was an experiment of a couple bored Solars. Solar A summons one and tells it to try to kill Solar B and, the demon being little real threat, Solar B messes with it for a century or so letting it build up charms. Finally the usurpation happens and Solar A dies, freeing the demon, which then kills wounded Solar B when he stumbles home barely escaping the Sidereals, does a little happy dance and disappears into the world keeping all his potent solar charms and generally being a menace to anyone on Creation he encounters from then on. Instant Big Bad for solar group in the new age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12171-kaiyen","name":"Kaiyen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T21:21:26-07:00","id":1300464,"title":"","content":"The Metody has no disguise skill. Does that imply that even when commanded to not look deformed/twisted it looks like an odd brown liquid person (appearance 1)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T05:04:36-07:00","id":1300516,"title":"","content":"Unless it strikes up a rivalry with a master of disguise, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T05:23:19-07:00","id":1300519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1300206-adversaries-the-quaghead-tribe-and-boscu-hundred-devils-metody?p=1300287#post1300287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read <i>Games of Divinity</i>, I visualized it as a violet liquid with a greasy rainbow sheen like oil on water. Not sure to what extent we'll want to describe its exact appearance when we get a chance to cover the Demon City in detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actual Oil of Vitriol (aka Sulfuric Acid) is a colourless, odourless syrup... until it reacts with metals to produce colourful metal sulfate solutions.<br /> <br /> So, if you look to the sulfu