"date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T07:59:29-07:00","id":1301625,"title":"","content":"I. I am scarred of the Metody. I am very scared of an elder metody, having survived eons, it's lair full of broken swords of consumed champions, as terrible as a glowering sun.<br /> <br /> ...that does remind me. If a Metody can get signature charms (I'm assuming even Exalted charms?), do they become 'non-summonable'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T09:56:04-07:00","id":1301664,"title":"","content":"I don't think so per-se, but when summoning, you just summon a random Metody, so the chances of getting one with some extra stuff isn't particularly likely. They might have a couple of extra dots or something.<br /> <br /> Possibly you can summon a particular demon by name, but this edition hasn't really gone into the nitty-gritty of summoning yet. I do feel though that you should be able to resummon a First Circle demon you had before, or maybe find some notable ones in an ancient grimoire of demon names, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:31:48-07:00","id":1301684,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely let someone use Demon of the Second Circle to summon a specific first circle if they really wanted to.<br /> <br /> Not sure if the timing requirements would remain the same...<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could give first circles of extraordinary power a charm that makes them count as a second circle for summoning...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-01-2019, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:31:35-07:00","id":1301701,"title":"","content":"Oh my god - Summon SPECIFIC Demon of of a First Circle species is a perfect Control effect for Summon Demon of the First Circle!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:16:53-07:00","id":1301758,"title":"","content":"So, I honestly want to know more about the laws of this realm and what sort of Thaumaturgy might be justified by it. Because that sounds pretty neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:45:25-07:00","id":1301765,"title":"","content":"Demon of the First Circle is described as calling a demon of the sorcerer's choice; I see no reason for that to not include a specific personage known to the summoner, so long as it's not trying to do anything silly like summon according to a broad category rather than knowing what or whom you're asking for.<br /> <br /> So like, you could call a specific metody that you're aware of having cultivated a certain broad array of powers with just the conventional spell, no bells and whistles attached, but doing so requires investigation of sorcerous lore, exploration of Malfeas, or interrogation of other demons to know whom you're asking for; you can't just cast the spell and say &quot;bring me a metody that knows a few water elemental Charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, I would imagine that a First Circle Demon of particular puissance, maybe as low as Essence 5 and any conceivable ones that are higher, should only be valid targets for the Celestial spell to call. That's presuming that there is still a capacity for First Circles to ascend in power.<br /> <br /> But that shouldn't be a metody that has acquired one or two Exalted Charms through determination and cunning and just a bit of luck. <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that the most powerful metody might be those who effectively market their skills in Creation, such that they were frequently summoned to be utilised in the feuds of the Exalted. The problem is the point at which they're getting powerful enough that many summoners become wary of employing them, if it's liable to be a point at which pursuing their own agenda causes a lot more collateral damage than is typical of those demons.<br /> <br /> That and, when they go home, they've got to be wary of higher ranked demons that might put them down for their presumption.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that the idea of an incredibly old one who has survived and thrived throughout numerous vendettas over ages, accumulating a library of additional powers, and living in utmost secrecy is mostly the kind of thing that metody and other demons tell one another as folk tales and hearsay (and occasionally ideals to compare themselves against and aspire to, for other metody), rather than anything unambiguously known or openly stated to exist. <br /> <br /> It's a lot like occasionally trading stories of how the Cataphract of Keys is actually a series of Exalted in elaborate disguise, although fewer demons take that one seriously; it's mostly just employed as a bit of bawdy revelry during some of the rowdier parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}